What does a Senior Product Information Specialist do at&nbsp;WPP Production? &nbsp;

The Senior Product Information Specialist acts as a critical verifier of relevant vehicle facts, product accuracy, and general product compliance for all agency communications for their assigned vehicles. This role reviews and provides direction on all images, claims, functionality, and messaging in each communication. The Senior Product Information Specialist also ensures that critical product information is proactively provided in advance for these communications, including digital, brand, paid and earned media opportunities. &nbsp;

They review all agency communications for assigned vehicles, emphasis is put on applied product information skills for content creation within the digital space - including model year PDM updates, MYCO site updates,&nbsp;Color&nbsp;and Trim projects, the maintenance of associated product grids and specifications, and securing samples and reference to provide visual direction to teams on any corrections or updates needed.&nbsp;

In addition, they also ensure that vehicle claims, material samples, and associated carryover items are updated, filed and accessible to a wide agency and client team throughout the lifecycle of the products they are assigned. &nbsp;

Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Investigate,&nbsp;retain, and apply robust vehicle knowledge for client and agency use. Ensure all communications associated with assigned vehicles are reviewed and commented upon accurately and within deadlines&nbsp;

• Mentor other team members appropriately&nbsp;

• Provide updates of carryover vehicles - including What’s New documents, claim updates and re-substantiation, PDM or other asset updates,&nbsp;Color&nbsp;and Trim changes and updates, and other related tasks associated with carryover vehicles&nbsp;

• Actively engage and understand all agency workflows so work can be commented upon and otherwise reviewed for product accuracy on time with proper project resolution. Emphasis on MYCO assignments, Build and Price reviews and Model/Options/Specs creation and verification&nbsp;

• Active preparation and participation in product-related client deliverables, including Owner Site,&nbsp;Color&nbsp;and Trim, and sample and reference materials needed for CG updates and validation&nbsp;

• Provide critical feedback to Product Information Supervisor for departmental improvements and progress&nbsp;

• Ensure&nbsp;accurate&nbsp;depictions of cross-brand technologies like Ford Pass, SYNC, and other technologies/connected services are compliant within your vehicles&nbsp;

